              <p>A client in Wallingford wanted wainscoting to match the original millwork in her 1910 farmhouse's front hall, but the exact profile was long out of production. We had a custom knife ground to match the original panel-and-rail dimensions rather than substituting a close modern equivalent. It cost more and took longer, but the new sections are indistinguishable from the century-old originals &mdash; which is the only bar that matters on historic trim work.</p>
